1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:07,255
To load a list, open Content, Import and choose Lead.

2
00:00:07,255 --> 00:00:12,080
The Columns Requirements table shows the columns a file can carry:

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:18,850
the lead status, source, list, company, rating and owner, next to the name and contact methods.

4
00:00:19,329 --> 00:00:23,744
Skip numbers that already belong to a contact leaves out rows whose number

5
00:00:23,744 --> 00:00:27,220
a contact has, so a customer is not called as a stranger.

6
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:31,193
Skip numbers that already belong to an open lead does the same for

7
00:00:31,193 --> 00:00:33,069
leads you are still working.

8
00:00:33,069 --> 00:00:34,669
Both are on by default.

9
00:00:35,191 --> 00:00:39,920
List name, Lead source, Lead status and Lead owner are given to every

10
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:42,821
new lead whose row does not set its own.

